# The build context. Everything the image needs is copied by name in infra/Dockerfile;
# what is listed here would otherwise be sent to the daemon, and a stale copy of a built
# artifact from a developer's working tree could shadow what the build produces.
#
# A pattern with no leading **/ matches at the root of the context alone, and `COPY packages/`
# copies whatever sits below it, so a pattern that names a kind of file starts with **/.

**/.git
**/.github
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.egg-info
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov

# The frontend is built inside the image, from source only.
**/node_modules
**/dist
packages/dirigent-server/frontend/e2e
packages/dirigent-server/frontend/shots
packages/dirigent-server/frontend/playwright-report
**/test-results
packages/dirigent-server/src/dirigent_server/static

**/.claude
**/.dirigent
**/.playwright-mcp
docs
site
reports

# A secret in the working tree is never build input.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
